📮 Reliving History, One Postcard at a Time! ✉️

A journey back in time, where handwritten letters carried emotions and postage stamps told stories of history and heritage!

On 14 October 2026, the Air Force Families Welfare Association (Regional), Headquarters Central Air Command, in collaboration with the Department of Posts and the Philatelic Society, organised a Philatelic Exhibition at the historic Old Post Office, Bamrauli, Prayagraj.

Set against the nostalgic backdrop of the vintage building, the exhibition brought India's rich postal heritage alive for young minds. A special display of First Day Covers and postage stamps highlighted the historical significance of Bamrauli Airfield, its association with early airmail services and the region's rich aviation heritage.

Children enthusiastically participated in postcard painting and experienced the forgotten charm of writing inland letters to their friends and families. Adding a heartfelt touch, the Department of Posts undertook to deliver these handwritten letters to their loved ones, creating memories to cherish.

The exhibition also offered a fascinating glimpse into India's philatelic heritage, fostering creativity, cultural awareness and an appreciation for traditional communication.

✨ More than an exhibition, it was a beautiful bridge between the past and present - reminding the younger generation that even in today's digital world, handwritten letters carry emotions that technology can never replace. 💌

